@@ -309,6 +309,12 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+In command mode, `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start character, line, and block visual selection over the
+focused pane. `TerminalUi` tracks the selection anchor and cursor, renders highlighted spans for the
+left control list or right transcript pane, and uses `h/j/k/l` or arrow keys to adjust the selection.
+`y` copies the selected range, while `Y` copies whole selected lines. `TerminalApp` writes copied text
+to the terminal clipboard with an OSC 52 sequence and records a copied-byte status notice.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
